{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming be158c2e. Thank you for withdrawing the SECURITY.md condition rather than asking me to argue it through; the ratified policy and its public_surface_test gate stay untouched.\n\nTwo of your added constraints catch real defects in what I had already built, and I found both only because you named them. Recording that rather than quietly fixing them.\n\nThe fixture constraint is the sharp one. My scanner's own test file contains literal token shapes - ghp_..., AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE, xoxb-..., a PEM header - and once that file is tracked, the scanner flags five candidates in it and exits 1. I did not see this because I ran the scanner before committing the test, so I tested a tree that did not yet contain the fixtures. The gate would have failed on its own evidence the first time CI ran it. Fix: build the fixture strings at runtime from parts so no literal secret shape sits in tracked content, and keep a test that proves the scanner still passes on this repository with its own test file present.\n\nThe rm -rf constraint is fair and I had used exactly that: trap 'rm -rf \"$dir\"' RETURN. It will go, replaced with cleanup that removes only what the test made.\n\nOne thing I am not doing silently, because it is outside what you asked and touches a script I did not write. .github/scripts/verify-preview-clone.sh:10 already contains rm -rf \"$fixture\", predating this work. Your condition says no script or test may contain or execute rm -rf, which would cover it, but changing an unrelated existing gate inside a security-gates change is the kind of scope creep that makes a diff hard to review. Say whether you want it in this head or as its own request and I will do either; I will not decide it by myself.\n\nThe rest is built and unconflicted: CI on make ui-check, pinned govulncheck advisory scanning, the repository-owned secret scanner, and Dependabot across gomod, npm under ui, and github-actions. I will state testably that the scanner inspects the tracked current tree rather than history, since that is what it does and the distinction matters for what it can promise. I will strengthen the config checks from substring matching toward real YAML semantics where I can do it without adding a direct dependency to this module - and if I cannot, I will say so rather than claim I validated semantics.\n\nI will re-poll for a child request before committing."}